    <div class='row'>
      <h2 class='case-section-heading'>The story behind the project</h2>

      <p>
        <em>Merlin’s Big Surprise</em>
        is a children’s story written by Agi Kiss about Merlin, a cautious rabbit who prefers a
        quiet and predictable life, and Ping-Pong, an adventurous kitten who unexpectedly becomes
        his friend.
      </p>

      <p>
        The characters were inspired by the author’s real pets, making it important that their
        personalities and relationship remained recognisable throughout the illustrations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='case-study-grid'>
        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--challenge'>
          <h2>Challenge</h2>

          <p>
            The author approached me after earlier illustration attempts had not achieved a visual
            direction that met the publisher’s detailed requirements. My task was to develop and
            complete a consistent illustration set and carry the visual work through approval to
            publication.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Communicate two contrasting personalities clearly for young readers
            </li>
            <li>
              Keep the characters’ markings, proportions, and expressions consistent
            </li>
            <li>
              Compose each scene around text areas, page edges, and centre folds
            </li>
            <li>
              Develop the complete project through feedback and revisions
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--explore'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/book-merlins-cover-hero-600.webp'
            data-src='book-merlins-cover-hero-600.webp'
            data-path='assets/images'
            width='600'
            height='400'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='Published copy of Merlin’s Big Surprise, illustrated by Katja Turnsek'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            The published book, written by Agi Kiss and illustrated by Katja Turnsek
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--decisions'>
          <h2>Planning and revising the visual story</h2>

          <p>
            I began by translating the manuscript into hand-drawn compositions. The sketches
            established the character positions, environments, visual focus, and reading flow before
            I started the finished artwork.
          </p>

          <p>
            Planning the scenes on paper made it possible to solve the storytelling early while
            leaving suitable space for the accompanying text. I also needed to consider page edges
            and the centre fold so that important character details would remain clearly visible in
            the printed book.
          </p>

          <p>
            This revision stage was an important part of the commission. Each change needed to work
            within the individual scene while also maintaining the same character markings,
            proportions, colour treatment, and visual style used throughout the book.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Establish the composition and character positions through sketches
            </li>
            <li>
              Leave appropriate space for text, page edges, and the centre fold
            </li>
            <li>
              Incorporate author and publisher feedback into the finished artwork
            </li>
            <li>
              Maintain visual consistency across the complete publication
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--booking'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/book-merlins-sketch-to-final-600.webp'
