            width='600'
            height='839'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='Pencil composition and finished digital illustration created for Merlin’s Big Surprise'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            A page composition developed from traditional sketches into finished digital artwork
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <h2 class='case-section-heading'>From sketch to finished artwork</h2>

      <p>
        After establishing each composition, I scanned the sketches and developed the final
        illustrations in Adobe Photoshop using a drawing tablet. I refined the characters,
        expressions, textures, lighting, colours, and environmental details while preserving the
        structure of the original drawings.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='case-study-grid'>
        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--challenge'>
          <h2>Traditional sketch</h2>

          <p>
            This drawing established Merlin’s pose, the window, and the surrounding room before
            digital painting began. It also helped define where the illustration needed detail and
            where quieter space should remain.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Establish the character’s pose and expression
            </li>
            <li>
              Plan the surrounding environment
            </li>
            <li>
              Resolve the composition before digital production
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--explore'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/book-merlins-sketch-600.webp'
            data-src='book-merlins-sketch-600.webp'
            data-path='assets/images'
            width='600'
            height='528'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='Traditional pencil and coloured-pencil sketch of Merlin sitting by a window'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            The original hand-drawn composition used to plan the window scene
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--decisions'>
          <h2>Digital production</h2>

          <p>
            The final illustration retained the original composition while developing the scene
            through colour, texture, lighting, and depth. Working digitally allowed me to refine the
            character’s fur, markings, and expression while keeping the softness of the original
            drawing.
          </p>

          <p>
            The open area around Merlin was kept intentionally restrained so that the finished
            illustration could work together with the book’s text and page layout.
          </p>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--booking'>
          <img
