            alt='Finished Photoshop illustration of Merlin sitting by a window'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            The completed Photoshop illustration developed from the original sketch
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <h2 class='case-section-heading'>Printed storytelling</h2>

      <p>
        The completed spreads show how the illustrations work together with the story text. Some
        scenes focus on quieter character moments, while others use action and more detailed
        environments to change the pace and guide the reader through the story.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='case-study-grid'>
        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--challenge'>
          <h2>Character and personality</h2>

          <p>
            Merlin’s cautious nature and Ping-Pong’s curiosity needed to remain visible through
            their expressions, poses, and interactions. The cherry-tree scene uses the characters’
            positions and eye lines to make their contrasting personalities immediately clear.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Merlin remains grounded and hesitant
            </li>
            <li>
              Ping-Pong occupies the more adventurous position
            </li>
            <li>
              The spread balances illustration with readable text areas
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--explore'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/book-merlins-cherry-spread-600.webp'
            data-src='book-merlins-cherry-spread-600.webp'
