          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            Merlin and Ping-Pong’s contrasting personalities shown in the cherry-tree chapter
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--decisions'>
          <h2>Consistency across the book</h2>

          <p>
            Maintaining recognisable characters across different environments and emotional
            situations was an important part of the project. Their markings and proportions needed
            to remain consistent whether they appeared in a quiet interior or an action scene.
          </p>

          <p>
            The fishpond spread also required a more complex environment with water, plants, a frog,
            movement, and interaction between both main characters.
          </p>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--booking'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/book-merlins-fishpond-spread-600.webp'
